12. Thus, the legal position that emerges from the aforesaid precedents interpreting Rule 37 and other provisions of the 1954 Act is :
(i) If the package containing article of food or label on the package bears any statement, design or device regarding the ingredients or the substances contained therein which is false or misleading in any material particular or if the package is otherwise deceptive w.r.t. its contents, the same would mean 'misbranding';
(ii) 'Misbranded' food is prohibited;
(iii) Rule 37 of the Rules framed under 1954 Act prohibits label from containing any statement, claim, design, device, fancy name or abbreviation which is false or misleading in any particular concerning :
 (a) the food contained in the package; or  (b) the quantity; or  (c) the nutritive value; or  (d) in relation to place or origin of the said  food.
